      "text": "The increase from \\(N\\) to \\(M\\) is \\(M-N.\\) Dividing by the original quantity and multiplying by \\(100\\) gives \\[ \\frac{100(M-N)}{N}. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
